{
 "note": "The Good Olive building and the Dome building, the two-storey pair on the east side of Bussell Hwy opposite the Visitor Centre, at the north end of the shops (Main Street Historic Walk sites 12 and 13; both modern, 1990s-2003). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and 2019 street photos. North: a two-storey L-shaped building with a pale grey hip roof and a deep two-storey verandah on white posts along the street, an upper balcony with a white balustrade and glazed upper rooms; the ground floor has The Good Olive. South: the Dome building, two storeys of sand-coloured render with tall upper windows (arched in reality), a flat roof behind a parapet, and a dark awning over the footpath. Behind and south of them, the rest of the same OSM footprint (a flat-roofed shop block and a barrel-roofed block) as plain outbuildings so the base doesn't lose them. Names in plain lettering, no logos. Metres: x left to right as seen from Bussell Hwy (north to south), y back (east) from the verandah line.",
